## CURRENT STATE
- D1 Professional Qualifications is independently verified for shipping on `d1-vinea-balance-complete`: the new lifecycle is separate from the frozen `20260825120000_profile_certifications.sql`, does not use `seller_verificato` as source of truth, and introduces no directory, search, bulk or probing endpoint.
- Migrations `20260827160000_d1_professional_qualifications.sql` and `20260827160500_d1_public_profile_qualifiche.sql` add owner-scoped qualification management, the private `professional-qualifications` bucket, an append-only private review ledger, the service-role-only idempotent review RPC, and the D8 public profile projection with the canonical green check plus the five-field badge allowlist.
- Lifecycle `bozza -> inviata -> approvata/rifiutata/ritirata` is enforced in PostgreSQL. The browser cannot approve or review; raw payload/reasoning is not owner-readable; documents and `storage_path` remain private; draft deletion reports success only after both the Storage object and metadata are removed.
- The canonical green check requires at least one `approvata` qualification whose `expires_on` is null or not before `current_date`. `/account` exposes the independent “Qualifiche professionali” panel and `/profilo/[id]` consumes only the canonical public projection.
- Disposable PostgreSQL verification passed 75/75 cases with all 9 residue counters at zero and the container/volume removed. `frontend-next` passed 91/91 targeted tests, typecheck, 1146/1146 full-suite tests across 72 files, the production build, and `git diff --check`.
- The CI floor is deliberately raised from `MIN_TESTS = 1092` to `MIN_TESTS = 1146`, matching the measured passing suite.
- No production fixture, qualification, document, provider call, API key, background worker or AI approval was created; the provider-neutral trusted review boundary remains OFF.

